    "pathway_role_summary": "DVL1 is a central cytoplasmic scaffold protein in both canonical and non-canonical Wnt signaling pathways. In canonical Wnt signaling, DVL1 is recruited to the plasma membrane upon Wnt ligand binding to Frizzled/LRP6 receptor complexes, where it facilitates disassembly of the beta-catenin destruction complex (APC/AXIN/GSK3B), allowing beta-catenin to accumulate and translocate to the nucleus to activate TCF/LEF-dependent transcription. In non-canonical Wnt pathways, DVL1 mediates planar cell polarity signaling and Wnt/Ca2+ signaling through interactions with Rho GTPases and other effectors. DVL1 is also subject to tight regulation through phosphorylation (by CK1ε and other kinases), ubiquitination (by KLHL12 and other E3 ligases leading to degradation), and acetylation (promoting nuclear translocation). The protein plays critical roles in development including neural tube closure, heart morphogenesis, axon guidance, and neuromuscular junction formation."
  },
