      "disease": "Robinow syndrome, autosomal dominant 2 (DRS2)",
      "omim_id": "616331",
      "mutation_type": "Germline frameshift mutations",
      "description": "Frameshift mutations in exon 14 of DVL1 cause autosomal dominant Robinow syndrome characterized by skeletal dysplasia, limb shortening, genital hypoplasia, and distinctive facial features. All identified pathogenic variants occur in exon 14 and result in premature termination with addition of >100 abnormal highly basic C-terminal amino acids. These mutants show increased canonical Wnt activity in vitro. At least 15 different DVL1 mutations have been identified in Robinow syndrome patients."
