    "modeling_relevance_summary": "DVL1 is a critical hub protein in Wnt signaling pathways, making it essential for modeling cellular responses to Wnt ligands. Key features for modeling: (1) Oligomerization through DIX domain creates signalosomes that amplify Wnt signals; (2) Multiple PTMs (phosphorylation, ubiquitination, acetylation) provide regulatory switches; (3) Scaffold function coordinates destruction complex disassembly; (4) Dual role in canonical (beta-catenin) and non-canonical (PCP, Ca2+) pathways; (5) Regulated degradation by KLHL12 provides negative feedback; (6) Membrane recruitment upon receptor activation is spatially regulated. The intrinsically disordered regions enable dynamic conformational changes and multiple protein-protein interactions. For Kappa modeling, focus on: DVL1 recruitment to membrane-bound Frizzled/LRP6, oligomerization states, phosphorylation-dependent activation, interaction with AXIN/APC destruction complex, and ubiquitin-mediated degradation dynamics."
